# Auto-created as `.gitignore` by the root `.envrc`. This template is tracked;
# the generated `.gitignore` is untracked and ignores itself, so a repo
# adopting this layout keeps whatever `.gitignore` it already has (the
# auto-create skips an existing file).
.gitignore

# Build products of the user layer: .direnv is direnv's own cache, .venv is
# created by `uv sync`, result* by a nix build.
.direnv
.venv
result
result-*

# Local direnv fragments, auto-created from their templates
.envrcs/.envrc.secrets
.envrcs/.envrc.user

# Per-user dotenv fragments (third layer) and plaintext secret sources.
# Plaintext never gets committed, so the wildcard is deliberately broad.
.envrcs/.env.*
.env
*.env

# Tracked exceptions, applied after the rules above:
#  - the templates, which the wildcard would otherwise hide from a fresh clone
#  - sops-encrypted bundles: an encrypted artifact is safe to commit, and
#    committing it is what lets a clone reach a working environment
!.envrcs/.env.*.template
!*.sops-encrypted
